{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3096","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3096","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3096\",\"parent_revision\":\"b88613e6b25255f20cc2fdd631024eef84cb408a791032b11b9e4924a2ac9aef\",\"root_revision\":\"b88613e6b25255f20cc2fdd631024eef84cb408a791032b11b9e4924a2ac9aef\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `complete-implementation` skill (`plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md`) has no step that opens a PR and no step that monitors a PR for reviews after work lands. Confirmed by direct read: SKILL.md's \\\"Final Step: Commit and Push Remaining Changes\\\" section commits and pushes to a branch, then proceeds straight to \\\"Final Handoff Output\\\" (`references/final-handoff.md`) \u2014 neither file contains any `gh pr create`, \\\"pull request\\\", or review-related step.\\n\\nThe workflow must be updated so that, as part of completing an implementation:\\n\\n1. A PR is opened for the work if one does not already exist.\\n2. After opening (or once an existing PR is confirmed), the agent must monitor that PR for CI status, review comments, and inline code suggestions \u2014 polling until CI completes and reviews have had a chance to land, not declaring done immediately after push.\\n3. Each review finding (bot or human) must be assessed against the actual current source and the task's original goal/acceptance criteria before acting on it \u2014 never blindly accepted or blindly dismissed.\\n4. Confirmed findings must be fixed, and dismissed findings must have their rebuttal reasoning stated.\\n5. After any fix, the same PR must be re-checked (CI re-run, no new unaddressed findings) before the loop is considered closed.\\n6. This monitor-assess-act-verify cycle repeats until the PR is clean, not a single pass.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: \\\"This is the same discipline already used manually, repeatedly, in this session's PR work (dispatching a fork to poll gh pr checks and gh api .../comments with --paginate, verifying each bot finding against real source before fixing or rebutting it, re-verifying after every fix round, only merging once clean) \u2014 it needs to be a codified step in complete-implementation's own pipeline, not something the orchestrating agent has to remember to do manually each time.\\\"\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: complete-implementation must open and monitor a pr through review to closure** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"90d4634096fcd659bdcf6069e81fa52d10ae3b8b01c2b74085f65a15ce16cb26\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP84tHQ\"}"}